  "title": "# AmberX app walkthrough video, like the one on demo.amberxai.com (Brett, Nov 1 ~3 AM) Read CLAUDE.…",
  "asked": "# AmberX app walkthrough video, like the one on demo.amberxai.com (Brett, Nov 1 ~3 AM) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/persona.md. Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. Brett: demo.amberxai.com has a long walkthrough (~17 min, link/player at the bottom of the page). He wants a walkthrough JUST LIKE THAT for the AmberX app. 1. Find how the demo walkthrough was made, WITHOUT downloading or viewing the site's adult media: look on this server for Walkthrough Studio (container walkthrough-studio, node:22) and the tour recorder (image amberx-tour-recorder, containers tour-rec / amberx-tour-rec), their source folders, project/data files, scripts, chapter lists, narration/TTS config and output settings. Also the demo site's page markup only (curl the HTML, no media) to see how the walkthrough player is embedded at the bottom. Reuse the same tooling, format and player. Write down what you found. 2. Make the AmberX walkthrough with that tooling: a script covering every main part of AmberX (web + Android shell where possible): home, approvals (Approve now / Deny / who asked / expandable rows / Watch live), command center, dictate + voice notes (note saved once), ask my notes, terminal, settings (Quiet switch, hide sensitive screens, appearance), the audio output recorder + session recording, agent Molly, overlay, hub links. Chapters with titles, plain-English narration in an Amber voice (Rhode Island attitude, clean, short), on-screen highlights of the control being explained. Length: as long as it needs, target 10-20 min, chapters skippable. 3. Record against the live AmberX web (amberx.amberxai.com) with a test/demo account or seeded demo data. NEVER show real secrets, keys, tokens, passwords, private notes or the sign-in; blur/mask anything sensitive. Phone layout (412x915) primary. 4. Put it in AmberX: a 'Walkthrough' entry at the bottom of Home and in the app menu + Help, opening the player with chapters (same player as the demo). If the help-mode build (branch claude/help-mode) has landed, link chapters from Help mode tooltips ('Watch how'). Video file stored on the server/hub, not committed to git if large (> 20 MB): commit the script/chapters/config, store the media where Walkthrough Studio keeps outputs and serve it through the existing auth. 5. Make it rebuildable: one command (and a console button) re-records the walkthrough when the UI changes. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only. Tests: walkthrough entry renders, player loads chapters, script validates, no secrets in frames (scan the recording's text with OCR or the DOM snapshots for key-like strings). Local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks. Screenshots of the entry + player (phone + desktop) to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'AmberX walkthrough - Nov 1'. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Report at _claude/builds/reports/amberx-walkthrough.md: how the demo one was made, chapter list, video length + where it's stored, how to re-record. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
